00:18:42.090 --> 00:18:44.070
And I am also giving it hints

00:18:44.070 --> 00:18:46.320
about what is the
structure of my code base.

00:18:46.320 --> 00:18:48.300
So you're going to see that one

00:18:48.300 --> 00:18:50.610
of the most important things
you can do as a data engineer,

00:18:50.610 --> 00:18:52.710
especially when you have a
very complex code base --

00:18:52.710 --> 00:18:56.610
so, for example, here you can
see we have a Scala-based code

00:18:56.610 --> 00:18:58.800
base; and the code
base is quite complex.

00:18:58.800 --> 00:19:01.560
There's at least a few
hundred thousand lines

00:19:01.560 --> 00:19:03.030
