00:19:03.030 --> 00:19:06.660
So, basically, we have hundreds
and hundreds of lines of code

00:19:06.660 --> 00:19:08.670
that are used in order to serve

00:19:08.670 --> 00:19:12.210
up the SQL Server OneLake
data lake, right?

00:19:12.210 --> 00:19:13.590
So this just keeps on going.

00:19:13.590 --> 00:19:15.960
So what you don't want to do
is you don't want Copilot

00:19:15.960 --> 00:19:19.260
to just go ahead and discover
all of this code every time

00:19:19.260 --> 00:19:21.510
