00:19:25.470 --> 00:19:27.990
The way we write our code is
we use these loader classes,

00:19:27.990 --> 00:19:29.820
transformer classes,
and driver classes.

00:19:29.820 --> 00:19:34.170
And you want to go ahead,
Copilot, and reuse as much code

00:19:34.170 --> 00:19:37.140
as possible; run unit
tests; run the Spark jobs;

00:19:37.140 --> 00:19:41.070
and then basically vacuum the
table so that, in production,

00:19:41.070 --> 00:19:43.650
we have the table
in a good format.

00:19:43.650 --> 00:19:45.120
So we give some context.

00:19:45.120 --> 00:19:48.870
You go ahead and tell Copilot
exactly what your coding pattern

00:19:48.870 --> 00:19:50.850
is in your particular repo.

00:19:50.850 --> 00:19:53.280
And, while it's reading the
skill, you can basically see

00:19:53.280 --> 00:19:56.700
that it picks up exactly
what the context is.

00:19:56.700 --> 00:19:59.880
At this point, you just
have to basically go ahead

00:19:59.880 --> 00:20:04.650
and tell AI some sort of visual
cue where it knows to stop.

00:20:04.650 --> 00:20:07.080
And you can see it's going
ahead and telling me, okay.

00:20:07.080 --> 00:20:09.360
What bronze tables do you want
to transform to silver, right?

00:20:09.360 --> 00:20:12.690
Go ahead and provide the full
database and table name.

00:20:12.690 --> 00:20:15.300
So, in this case,
as I mentioned,

00:20:15.300 --> 00:20:16.440
we have Spark running locally.

00:20:16.440 --> 00:20:19.460
So you can see I've got
Apache Spark is running

00:20:19.460 --> 00:20:21.020
