00:20:30.560 --> 00:20:32.930
and using local Spark
to query OneLake.

00:20:32.930 --> 00:20:34.520
These are the tables
that we have in OneLake.

00:20:34.520 --> 00:20:36.770
So just as an example, you know,
let's say I want to go ahead

00:20:36.770 --> 00:20:40.370
and do a bronze transformation
on this particular table,

00:20:40.370 --> 00:20:42.660
on this Arc SQL
Server extension log.

00:20:42.660 --> 00:20:48.090
So all I have to do is go
ahead and just place it.

00:20:48.090 --> 00:20:48.840
So I have this query.

00:20:48.840 --> 00:20:51.990
Let me just go ahead and
copy it and paste it here,

00:20:51.990 --> 00:20:53.520
and then I click on run.

00:20:53.520 --> 00:20:55.710
And what this is doing
is this is using Livy

00:20:55.710 --> 00:21:00.540
